# Errors of the {{ twin_name }} twin API

Every error is a JSON document with media type `application/problem+json`:

```json
{"type": "urn:dta:error:store.unknown_type", "title": "Unknown type", "status": 404,
 "detail": "…what was wrong…", "code": "store.unknown_type", "trace_id": "…"}
```

Branch on `code`, not on the text. Quote `trace_id` when you report a failure to the user: it finds the request in the twin's logs (`/lifecycle/logs?trace_id=…`).

| Status | Code | Meaning | What to do |
|---|---|---|---|
| 400 | `api.bad_request` | a parameter is missing, malformed or out of range | read `detail` and `errors` (each names the parameter), fix the request; for JSON the largest `limit` is 10,000 |
| 400 | `api.bad_cursor` | the cursor is not from this query | start the listing again without `cursor` |
| 400 | `api.slice_too_large` | the slice would be too large | narrow the range, add a step (`a..b/<step>`), or name fewer objects or properties |
| 400 | `store.bad_selector` | `at`, `from`, `to` or `range` is not a version selector | use `head`, a commit id, `#<n>`, an ISO time with an offset, or `<a>..<b>` |
| 400 | `store.naive_datetime` | a time has no offset | add `Z` or an offset such as `+01:00` (as `%2B01:00` in a URL) |
| 400 | `store.bad_time` | a time cannot be read | write it as ISO 8601 |
| 400 | `store.bad_filter` | a `where` clause is malformed, or its value does not fit the property's kind | `<property>:<op>:<value>`; check the property's kind in the schema |
| 400 | `store.bad_branch_name` | the branch name is not valid | list branches with `/history/branches` |
| 400 | `graph.too_broad` | the traversal would visit too much | lower `depth` or `limit`, or name `edge_types` |
| 400 | `graph.bad_edge_filter` | `edge_where` names a type that is not a link type and has none under it | take link types from the schema (`kind` `link`); for a property of an object type use `where` on a listing |
| 400 | `graph.bad_weight` | the weight is not a numeric property of the links on the path | choose a numeric link property from the schema, or leave `weight` out |
| 400 | `sync.unknown_source`, `sync.replay_unknown` | the request to start a run names a source or dataset the twin does not have | take source ids and dataset names from `/sync/sources` |
| 401 | `api.unauthorized` | the token is missing or wrong | check that `{{ token_env }}` is set and sent as a bearer token; ask the user if it is not |
| 404 | `api.not_found` | no such endpoint | check the path against `reference/api.md` |
| 404 | `api.unknown_object` | no object with that uid at that version | it may not exist yet, or no longer, at the version you asked for; check `at` |
| 404 | `store.unknown_type` | the schema has no such type at that version | read `/meta/schema` again at the same `at` |
| 404 | `store.unknown_property` | the type has no such property at that version | read `/meta/schema` again at the same `at` |
| 404 | `store.unknown_version` | no version matches the selector | list versions with `/history/versions`; a time before the first version matches nothing |
| 404 | `store.unknown_branch` | no such branch | list branches with `/history/branches` |
| 404 | `sync.run_not_found` | no run with that uid | take uids from `/sync/runs`; a uid is written whole, `twin_sync_run:…` |
| 404 | `sync.rejects_missing` | the file of rows a run set aside is no longer held | report it with the trace id; the run's counts are still in `/sync/runs` |
| 404 | `job.not_found` | no job with that id | jobs are forgotten when the API restarts and after 200 newer ones; look for the run in `/sync/runs` instead |
| 405 | `api.method_not_allowed` | wrong HTTP method | most endpoints are `GET`; the subgraph and starting a sync run are `POST` |
| 409 | `twin.not_live` | a run was asked of a static twin | a static twin does not sync; tell the user |
| 409 | `sync.busy` | a run with other parameters is queued or running | wait for the job in the answer's `job` (`/lifecycle/jobs/{id}`), then ask again if it is still needed |
| 409 | `sync.key_reused` | the `Idempotency-Key` was used before for a different request | use a new key for a new request |
| 422 | `store.violation` | data would break the schema's rules | does not arise from reading; report it with the trace id |
| 503 | `store.unavailable`, `store.closed`, `store.lock_timeout`, `store.not_installed` | the twin's store cannot answer now | wait a few seconds and retry up to three times; then tell the user the twin is down |
| 503 | `job.closed` | the API is stopping and starts no job | wait until the twin is up again, then ask again |
| 500 | `api.internal` | a fault in the twin | do not retry in a loop; report the trace id to the user |

A connection that is refused or times out means the twin's stack is not running or the address is wrong. Tell the user; do not look for the twin elsewhere.
